course: dictionary
lesson: 13924
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives leech four meanings: a small worm, a rude word for a person, and two verbs. Context, the words and sentences around it, tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «The leech stuck to the boy's leg as he waded through the pond.» The clues are pond and waded through, so a leech here is the small worm that sucks blood. Ask yourself: does the sentence still make sense if I use my meaning?
explain: «Dan leeches off his friends and never pays for a single thing.» Here leeches is a verb. Leeches off means uses other people to get what he wants and gives nothing back. A phrase like cling like a leech helps you remember this.
explain: «The cold slowly leeched the warmth from my hands.» Leeched means slowly took away. You can test it by swapping in slowly took away: the sentence still makes sense, so you know you have the right meaning.
fact: A leech is a small worm that lives in water or wet places.
fact: Leeches have suckers and feed on blood from animals and people.
fact: Long ago, doctors used leeches to take blood, and some doctors still use them today for special treatments.
fact: Calling a person a leech is rude, because it means they use other people and give nothing back.
fact: «Leeched» means slowly took something away, as in «the cold leeched the warmth from his hands».
exercise: «The leech swam in the muddy pond.» What is a leech in this sentence? | A kind of fish | *A small worm that sucks blood | A tall tree by the water | A bird that sings at dawn
exercise: «Sam leeches off his brother and never buys his own sweets.» What does leeches off mean? | Swims very fast in the sea | Feeds the birds in the park | *Uses others and gives nothing back | Shares everything fairly with others
exercise: «The cold leeched the warmth from his hands.» What does leeched mean? | Quickly added | *Slowly took away | Washed clean | Made warm again
test: «Ella is such a leech, always asking for help and never helping anyone back.» What does leech mean here? | A bird of the sea | A small worm in a pond | A kind teacher | *A person who uses others and gives nothing back
test: Which sentence uses leech as a verb? | A rainforest leech is very small. | Doctors used leeches long ago. | *The hot sun slowly leeched the juice from the fruit. | The leech lives in the pond.
exam: Dara says a leech is a fish that lives in the sea. Is she right? | Yes, leeches are fish that swim in the sea | No, a leech is a bird that sings at dawn | *No, a leech is a small worm that sucks blood | Yes, but only in rainforests
